  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual analogy as a speaker of the false equivalence",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the top text 'goats can't talk' as the originator or embodiment of the degrading analogy. The meme constructs a false equivalence by projecting the user's perspective onto the text, suggesting that the user is making or endorsing the claim that Muslim men are mute or incapable of reporting crimes, thereby aligning the user with the hateful stereotype. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but is implied through the meme's structure, where the user is expected to understand and accept the analogy as a valid framing of the issue.",
